{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_15-11-32-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nexp = {\n \\\"investigation_id\\\": \\\"f47677cc0dd94647aa374fc84b1e6b8e-question-1\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\": \\\"epaxos/assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n \\\"execution_package\\\": \\\"./epaxos\\\",\n \\\"test_names\\\": [\\\"TestAssuranceEPaxosRecoveryBallotProgress\\\"],\n \\\"anchors\\\": [\n   {\\\"material_id\\\": \\\"s-decl-recovery\\\", \\\"symbol\\\": \\\"startRecoveryForInstance\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 1127, \\\"end_line\\\": 1141},\n   {\\\"material_id\\\": \\\"s-decl-prepare-reply\\\", \\\"symbol\\\": \\\"handlePrepareReply\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 1204, \\\"end_line\\\": 1235}\n ],\n \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"s-makeballot\\\",\\\"s-decl-recovery\\\",\\\"s-decl-prepare-reply\\\",\\\"s-isleader-default\\\",\\\"s-betheleader\\\",\\\"s-exec-recovery-trigger\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\": {\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Five replicas (F=2) built and driven as in the value-adoption harness (in-process replicas with the package's own handlers and marshaled RPC structs, FIFO delivery, no delivery to crashed replicas). Scenario: replica 1 holds a conflicting command so the owner's pre-accept replies are not equal; owner replica 0 proposes X on its own instance (0,0) at ballot 0, enters the Accept phase and broadcasts Accept to replicas 1 and 2 (their AcceptReplies are left in flight, i.e. the owner is slow); replica 2 then recovers the same instance at its own ballot 7, so replicas 0, 1, 3 and 4 join ballot 7 and record bal 7, and replica 2 fails after broadcasting that Prepare; the owner then runs two ordinary startRecoveryForInstance(0,0) attempts (as its executor does after COMMIT_GRACE_PERIOD), and finally a third attempt after the target's own BeTheLeader handler is invoked on it, followed by completion of the quiescent exchange.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\": [\n   \\\"Replica construction mirrors epaxos.New minus peer connections, run() loop and ComputeClosestPeers; InstanceSpace rows hold 32 entries instead of MAX_INSTANCE, and only instance (0,0) is used.\\\",\n   \\\"The owner's AcceptReplies from replicas 1 and 2 are never delivered, modelling a slow owner whose recovery timers on the other replicas fire while the replies are in flight; the recovery of an instance whose owner is slow is a normal EPaxos event.\\\",\n   \\\"Replica 2's failure is modelled as: no further message is delivered to it, its queue is discarded and every replica's Alive flag for it is cleared.\\\",\n   \\\"Replica 1's conflicting command comes from a real startPhase1 whose auxiliary broadcast is discarded; only its local conflict state is used.\\\",\n   \\\"IsLeader is set through the target's own BeTheLeader handler, the same RPC the master invokes, and no production logic is modified.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"excluded\\\": [\\\"No client path, no state-machine execution, no run() loop or recovery timer loop in the harness.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\": {\\\"n\\\": 5, \\\"f\\\": 2, \\\"owner\\\": 0, \\\"other_recoverer\\\": 2, \\\"non_leader_ballot\\\": 0, \\\"higher_stored_bal\\\": 7, \\\"leader_ballot\\\": 10, \\\"slow_quorum\\\": 3}\n },\n \\\"prefix\\\": \\\"The harness drives the package's own startPhase1/bcastPreAccept/handlePreAcceptReply/bcastAccept path for the owner, injects the higher-ballot Prepare of replica 2 through handlePrepare at replicas 0, 1, 3 and 4, then calls startRecoveryForInstance(0,0) at the owner three times, delivering every emitted Prepare to the peers' handlePrepare and every PrepareReply back to the owner, and recording the owner's tried ballot, the peers' stored ballots, the appended reply count and any follow-up message. Between attempts 2 and 3 it invokes replica 0's own BeTheLeader handler.\\\",\n \\\"requirement\\\": \\\"Recovery authority must be acquirable by the replica that runs the recovery